Stimuli and derived data (data/, additional_Qs/*.csv, additional_Qs/accepted/, additional_Qs/slots/,
results/, additional_Qs/rq*/, additional_Qs/rq12_on_165/, additional_Qs/cf_rescue_*/,
additional_Qs/rpc_vector_control/) are released under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), with the following exception:
items chung-1 to chung-4 in data/stimuli_RQ3.csv adapt the published materials of
Chung, Dorst, Mandelkern and Mascarenhas (2024), and the three edited items reuse
hypotheses from Tentori, Crupi and Russo (2013); those texts remain the property of
their original authors and are reproduced here for research replication only.
The fluency-guard text (data/wikitext_rq3_guard.txt) is a 1,000-token excerpt of
WikiText-103 (Merity et al., 2017), CC BY-SA 3.0.
